    ​
    [head=1]CONTRACT[/head]
    ​
    Between [bold]SCP-049[/bold] (hereinafter referred to as the "Plague Doctor") and the [bold]SCP Foundation[/bold] (hereinafter referred to as the "Foundation")
    ​
    ​[head=3]1. PURPOSE OF THE AGREEMENT[/head]
    This contract establishes the rules for the maintenance, interaction, and limitations of the rights and responsibilities of the Plague Doctor and Foundation personnel. This document is aimed at ensuring the safety of personnel, preserving the scientific value of the facility, and preventing abuse of privileges by either party.
    ​
    ​[head=3]2. PARTIES AND DEFINITIONS[/head]
    ​[bullet][bold]Plague Doctor[/bold] is an object identified as SCP-049.
    ​[bullet][bold]The Foundation[/bold] is the organization responsible for the containment, study, and control of SCP-049.
    ​[bullet][bold]Foundation Personnel[/bold] - employees of the institution who have a key card indicating their clearance level and a record of their legitimacy in the personnel registry console.
    ​[bullet][bold]Emergency situation (ES)[/bold] is an event that poses an immediate threat to the life and/or integrity of an institution and/or personnel (breakthrough, armed conflict, etc.).
    ​
    ​[head=3]3. GENERAL PROVISIONS[/head]
    [bullet]The Plague Doctor has signed this contract and thereby confirms his understanding and acceptance of the terms and conditions contained herein.
    [bullet]Signing does not make the Plague Doctor an employee in the organizational sense; SCP-049 remains a containment object with the limited rights specified in this document.
    [bullet]The rights, privileges and responsibilities of the Plague Doctor are limited solely by the provisions of this contract and the decisions of the institution's management (institution director, head of the scientific service).
    ​
    ​[head=3]4. RIGHTS OF THE PLAGUE DOCTOR[/head]
    [bullet]The Foundation undertakes to provide basic conditions of detention: safety, food, medical support, and the ability to carry out approved research sessions under the supervision of staff.
    [bullet]The Plague Doctor is permitted to make written and oral statements to staff and scientists within the limits that do not contradict the instructions of the staff of the appropriate level (director of the institution, head of the scientific service, head of security).
    [bullet]Other privileges are granted only with the permission of the head of the scientific service or the director of the institution.
    ​
    ​[head=3]4.1. SPECIAL PERMISSIONS FOR SCP-049 REQUESTS[/head]
    Right to Request
    SCP-049 is authorized to make requests for restricted items and "patients" (D-Class personnel) only through personnel with Level 3 clearance or higher.
    ​
    Approved items for medical operations:
    [bullet]basic surgical instruments (scalpel, retractor, gloves, etc.);
    [bullet]simple medications (bruise kits, ointments, etc.) - strictly under the control of scientists or the Security Council;
    [bullet]Other items may be added to the list only with the written permission of the director of the institution or the head of the scientific service.
    ​
    [bold]Patients (class D)[/bold]
    [bullet]SCP-049 has the right to request the provision of test subjects (D-Class) for "operations" or research.
    [bullet]The number of D-classes provided simultaneously is determined by the director of the institution and cannot exceed the limit established by internal protocols.
    [bullet]All interactions between SCP-049 and D-class personnel occur exclusively under the supervision of scientists or security personnel.
    ​
    ​[bold]Restrictions and conditions[/bold]
    [bullet]SCP-049 does not have the authority to independently select specific D-Classes or items. This decision is made by Foundation personnel, with the exception of items permitted in Section 4.1 of the agreement.
    [bullet]Requests are reviewed on a routine basis and may be rejected without explanation in the event of a security threat, emergency, resource constraints, or at the discretion of management.
    [bullet]Providing items and patients is not a right of SCP-049, but merely an option available to it as long as it complies with containment and security regulations.
    ​
    [bold]Abuse and Violations[/bold]
    [bullet]If SCP-049 exhibits aggressive or manipulative behavior while submitting a request, it will lose the right to make further requests for a period of time determined by the Director or Head of Research.
    [bullet]Attempts to use the provided items or D-classes outside the scope of the experiment will result in immediate intervention by the Security Council, confiscation of the items, and the use of suppressive measures.
    ​
    ​[head=3]5. LIMITATIONS AND OBLIGATIONS OF THE PLAGUE DOCTOR[/head]
    [bullet]The Plague Doctor has no right to demand that personnel act in contravention of orders from the facility director, the head of the scientific service, or the Security Service. His words do not carry the force of an order.
    [bullet]The Plague Doctor undertakes not to take any action that may pose a threat to the lives of personnel or the integrity of the institution.
    [bullet]Manipulative, aggressive, or overtly demanding behavior on the part of the Plague Doctor is considered a violation of the terms and is considered grounds for disciplinary action.
    [bullet]In an emergency, the safety of staff and the facility takes precedence over the Plague Doctor's comfort; his requests and privileges may be temporarily and irrevocably suspended.
    ​
    ​[head=3]6. RESPONSIBILITIES AND RIGHTS OF THE FUND STAFF[/head]
    [bullet]Staff are required to treat the Plague Doctor with respect and professionalism, but without granting him "special status."
    [bullet]Staff are required to comply with the terms of the contract and follow protective instructions.
    [bullet]Security services have the right to apply restraining measures (suppression, amnestics, isolation, use of force) in cases of contract violation or when life/safety is threatened.
    [bullet]If attempts to escape or a significant violation of conditions are detected, the director of the institution and the head of the scientific service have priority in taking action.
    ​
    ​[head=3]7. EMERGENCY PROCEDURES[/head]
    [bullet]In the event of an immediate threat to the lives of personnel or a major breach, priority actions include: localization of the threat, suppression (lethal, non-lethal, as decided by the director of the institution or the head of security), isolation of the facility, and the use of amnestics and restorative procedures.
    [bullet]If the Plague Doctor is aggressive and fewer than two SCP-049-2 are present, the threat is considered controlled; if two or more SCP-049-2 are present, additional containment and fire protocols are implemented.
    ​
    ​[head=3]8. INFORMATION AND COMMUNICATION[/head]
    ​[bold]Privacy[/bold]
    [bullet]All internal Foundation information (radio communications, documents, protocols, personal employee records, internal reports) is classified and intended exclusively for personnel with the appropriate clearance level.
    [bullet]SCP-049 has no legal access to Foundation data, except for information directly transmitted to it through experiments or communication with personnel.
    ​
    [bold]Ban on the use of communication devices[/bold]
    [bullet]SCP-049 is prohibited from possessing or using headsets, radios, intercoms, terminals, or any other communication devices that allow the reception or transmission of personnel information.
    [bullet]Any communication device found on SCP-049 or in its containment chamber is to be immediately confiscated.
    ​
    [bold]Information Isolation[/bold]
    [bullet]Personnel are to ensure that SCP-049 does not have access to classified information.
    [bullet]In the event that SCP-049 accidentally witnesses or learns information not intended for it, said information is considered null and void for SCP-049 and cannot be used as an argument in requests or negotiations.
    ​
    Responsibility
    [bullet]Attempts by SCP-049 to use classified Foundation information (including blackmail or threats) are a breach of contract and will result in immediate suppression and temporary isolation.
    [bullet]Breaches of confidentiality by employees (for example, leaving a headset in a cell) are recorded as an official error, and the guilty personnel are subject to disciplinary action.
    ​
    ​[head=3]9. DISCIPLINARY MEASURES AND SANCTIONS[/head]
    [bullet]For violation of the terms of the contract, the Foundation has the right to apply one or more of the following measures: verbal warning, isolation, forced sedation, transfer to a high-security regime, temporary or permanent restriction of privileges.
    [bullet]In case of systematic or gross violations, lethal measures may be applied at the discretion of the director of the institution.
    ​
    ​[head=3]9.1. VIOLATION BY THE FUND[/head]
    In the event that Foundation personnel violate the terms of the contract (use excessive force, deprive SCP-049 of rights and privileges expressly stipulated in the contract, or ignore established agreements without an emergency), SCP-049 is granted the right to:
    ​
    ​[bullet]Submit a formal request through the designated curator (a scientist, head of the scientific service, or an authorized employee with level 3+ clearance).
    ​
    [bold]If the violation is confirmed:[/bold]
    [bullet]Foundation employees found guilty may be subject to disciplinary action (demotion, loss of security clearance, transfer to D-class, internal investigation).
    [bullet]SCP-049 receives compensation in the form of restoration of violated privileges and additional capabilities (e.g., one unscheduled research session, more freedom in requesting small inventory).
    ​
    [bold]In the event of systematic violations of the terms of the agreement by the Foundation’s staff:[/bold]
    [bullet]SCP-049 has the right to temporarily refuse to participate in testing/research until the conflict is resolved.
    [bullet]In this case, SCP-049 is required to remain within the containment chamber and not take any actions that threaten the safety of the facility.
    [bullet]In an emergency, Foundation actions that violate SCP-049's amenities or privileges are not considered a violation if they are directly aimed at saving the lives of personnel or containing a threat.
    ​
    ​[head=3]10. MODIFICATION AND TERMINATION OF THE CONTRACT[/head]
    [bullet]Any changes to the contract are made only with the written permission of the director of the institution and the approval of the head of the scientific service.
    [bullet]The contract may be terminated by the Director of the Facility in the event of systematic, gross violations by SCP-049 or a change in the object's status.
    [bullet]If the contract is terminated, all privileges of SCP-049 will be revoked and it will be transferred to standard containment.
